[ti:2-08-人生哲理类]
[00:00.00]As we can see from the picture,
[00:02.47]in a residence community with television antennas on the roof,
[00:07.72]an upset young man is talking to his friend walking beside him along the street.
[00:14.25]It is apparent that the former assumes that someone else is more qualified than him.
[00:21.18]Young people tend to give up when the problem is beyond their ability to cope with.
[00:27.91]Superficially,
[00:29.30]it seems to be somewhat reasonable,
[00:32.27]but when weighing in the mind,
[00:34.74]we find there is an apparent tendency behind this phenomenon: the lack of confidence.
[00:41.87]Firstly,
[00:42.66]it is well-known that we exist in a dynamic world with various difficulties.
[00:49.00]We can do nothing but face them.
[00:51.57]Secondly,
[00:52.47]attitude is the key point of taking the first step.
[00:56.62]Being equipped with bravery and confidence to solve the problem,
[01:02.07]you will find the question is not as “huge” as you imagine.
[01:06.82]So,
[01:07.12]with confidence and the right assessment of difficulties,
[01:12.07]try and exert our strength,
[01:14.34]and then we will overcome all the difficulties.
[01:18.30]On the whole,
[01:19.39]I believe we young people should face the difficulties in a right manner.
[01:25.43]And nothing is impossible to a willing mind.
